      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is a delegate?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A delegate is a type-safe function pointer that references methods with a specific signature, enabling callback methods and event handling."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Delegates hold references to methods. Can be single-cast or multi-cast. Action, Func, and Predicate are built-in delegate types. Foundation for events and LINQ."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Delegate Example",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "// Custom delegate\npublic delegate void Notify(string message);\n\n// Built-in delegates\nAction<string> action = msg => Console.WriteLine(msg);\nFunc<int, int, int> add = (a, b) => a + b;\nPredicate<int> isEven = n => n % 2 == 0;\n\n// Usage\naction(\"Hello\");\nvar result = add(2, 3);"
      }
    },
    {
